# The mainnet TUI's key references.
#
# Copy this file to `keys.env` beside it (git-ignored) and replace each
# placeholder with your own 1Password reference. Nothing here is a secret:
# every value is an `op://` *reference*, and `make tui-mainnet` points the TUI
# at the file with `--keys-file`. The TUI parses it itself and resolves each
# reference in memory with `op read`. Never `source` it, and never run the TUI
# under `op run`, either of which would put a resolved key into the process
# environment.
#
# A flag overrides its line for one launch (`--wallet`, `--leader`, `--quote`).
# Set DROPSET_OP_ACCOUNT in the shell when `op` is signed in to more than one
# account.
#
# This file holds signing keys only. The data stack's credentials live in the
# localnet collectors enclave (infra/localnet/secrets.local.env.example).

# Admin: registry admin, upgrade authority, fee payer. Required on mainnet.
DROPSET_TUI_WALLET=op://<vault>/<admin-item>/<field>

# Lead: the vault leader, the custody key, used by create-vault, deposit,
# withdraw and the emergency close and drain. It is resolved only when one of
# those steps first needs it, so a re-centre session never loads it.
DROPSET_TUI_LEADER=op://<vault>/<lead-item>/<field>

# Quote: the vault's quote authority, the hot-path key. It signs the passive
# ladder, the re-centre and the emergency kill, and create-vault sets it on
# every new vault. Required on mainnet.
DROPSET_TUI_QUOTE=op://<vault>/<quote-item>/<field>
